
# Olinda Vashi — Electronics & Computer Engineering Portfolio

## 1. Project Overview

This project is a professional portfolio website developed to showcase my background, engineering skills, projects, technical interests, and professional development as an Electronics and Computer Engineering student.

The portfolio presents my experience in electronics, embedded systems, software development, and engineering innovation. It is designed to provide potential employers, internship providers, collaborators, and other visitors with an overview of my technical abilities and projects.

The website includes:

- A home section introducing my professional profile.
- An About section describing my engineering journey.
- A Skills section presenting my technical competencies.
- A Projects section showcasing selected engineering projects.
- A GitHub Projects section that retrieves selected repositories using the GitHub API.
- A technical article section.
- A Contact section with client-side form validation.
- Light and dark theme functionality.
- A downloadable CV.

---

## 2. Project Objectives

The objectives of this portfolio are to:

1. Present my academic and engineering background professionally.
2. Showcase selected hardware, embedded systems, and software projects.
3. Demonstrate practical HTML, CSS, and JavaScript skills.
4. Apply responsive web design principles.
5. Implement accessibility and usability considerations.
6. Integrate a live API using JavaScript and async/await.
7. Practise collaborative development using Git and GitHub.
8. Provide a platform for future employers and collaborators to contact me.

---

## 3. Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| HTML5 | Semantic website structure |
| CSS3 | Styling, responsive layouts, and themes |
| JavaScript | Interactivity, form validation, and API integration |
| Git | Version control |
| GitHub | Repository hosting and collaboration |
| Figma | Wireframes, mockups, and design system |
| GitHub REST API | Retrieving selected repository information |

---

## 4. Main Features

### Responsive Design

The website is designed to adapt to desktop, tablet, and mobile screen sizes.

### Theme Toggle

Users can switch between light and dark themes. The selected theme is stored in local storage so that the preference can be remembered.

### Mobile Navigation

A navigation toggle allows users to access the website menu on smaller screens.

### Contact Form Validation

The contact form includes client-side validation to check the information entered by the user.

### GitHub API Integration

The website retrieves public repositories from my GitHub account and filters the results to display the following selected projects:

- Quotation System
- Fuel Level Monitoring System

The API integration includes loading and error states.

---

## 5. Featured Projects

The portfolio presents selected engineering projects, including:

- Soil Moisture Monitoring System
- Syringe Pump
- Kandodo Digital Level Meter

Additional repositories are displayed through the GitHub Projects section.

